config BR2_PACKAGE_EMBRA_MT7922_FIRMWARE
	bool "embra-mt7922-firmware"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE_MEDIATEK_MT7922
	help
	  The Wi-Fi firmware of MediaTek's MT7922 (the firmware and its
	  ROM patch) at the release of linux-firmware embraOS pins: the
	  version in embra-mt7922-firmware.mk, each file's sha256 in the
	  hash file beside it. The recipe installs the two files over
	  the ones of Buildroot's linux-firmware package, whose release
	  carries a file the kernel's driver refuses (the recipe's
	  comment has the account).

	  It goes when Buildroot's linux-firmware is 20251021 or later.

	  https://gitlab.com/kernel-firmware/linux-firmware
